Z||000012||rockcrawl||12-25-2001||09:04 PM||||The neat thing about DC motors is that they have nearly continuous torque from 0 RPM to max RPM. You can start out in third gear and not ever need to shift, the controller and SCRs do all the work. I've never seen an electric conversion with an auto trans, not sure how that would work, it would probably destroy the trans in no time at all. That GE EV-1 controller would probably need some major adjustments to work properly.||||reg||1
